        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T10:53:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  In case of lid being closed it might happen that state is wrongly read as opened. Only risk is 10s of led being on.\n\nI wouldn\u0027t call in negligible risk 😄 EC core code uses a LID_DEBOUNCE_US config. The simplest solution would be to use delayed work + checking state of GPIO, but not sure if I\u0027m missing something or not. What do you think? FPMCU should go sleep while LED is on, right?",
      "parentUuid": "40e650ab_f3983e49",
      "revId": "7ad1cc1ed94358be5c6cb130b6c9357aedbb233b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
